WEBVTT

00:57.474 --> 00:59.684
Here's the numbers.

00:59.768 --> 01:01.561
- Look at this chart.
- Go to check the center now.

01:02.979 --> 01:04.606
Look over here. Look at this.

01:04.689 --> 01:07.150
The direction headed over towards Japan.

01:07.233 --> 01:09.611
- Come on, Director. It can't be.
- It's coming in too strong.

01:09.694 --> 01:12.155
It's heading down from the north.
The temperature's following.

01:12.238 --> 01:14.657
So it's heading down
towards the southeast here.

01:14.741 --> 01:16.242
Is that what
the data says right now?

01:17.410 --> 01:18.536
Wait a second.

01:19.746 --> 01:21.122
- No.
- Look.

01:21.206 --> 01:23.625
Hey, hey, hey. The current data.

01:24.250 --> 01:25.418
It's flowing this way.

01:25.502 --> 01:28.379
Okay, and this one's… Okay, so it's there.

01:47.190 --> 01:49.484
TYPHOON RICKY CONTINUES TO
CAUSE DAMAGE IN VARIOUS LOCATIONS

01:49.567 --> 01:51.194
Yes, I understand.

01:51.277 --> 01:52.946
- Sir.
- Ah!

01:54.656 --> 01:58.576
Yes. Ah! Do the… do the…
the rainfall forecast again.

01:58.660 --> 02:00.745
- Yeah, right.
- Yeah? Yes?

02:07.001 --> 02:09.045
- Hey, could I have you look at this?
- Of course.

02:09.129 --> 02:10.130
Great.

02:11.589 --> 02:13.591
Okay.

02:15.176 --> 02:17.637
Yes, Team One here. Yes.

02:30.150 --> 02:34.070
Yesterday night, Typhoon Ricky
swept through the Korean Peninsula,

02:34.154 --> 02:35.947
wreaking havoc on the nation.

02:36.030 --> 02:39.784
Winds reached 30m per second,
resulting in a 120 injured or dead,

02:39.868 --> 02:43.454
causing 80 billion won in damages
across the Korean Peninsula.

02:43.538 --> 02:48.168
The downpour last night also caused
flooding and damage in many areas.

02:48.251 --> 02:50.086
- Today at dawn in Yangcheon-gu, Seoul…
- Whoa!

02:50.170 --> 02:52.797
- …firefighters are already…
- Looks like this time the KMA was right.

02:52.881 --> 02:53.965
…after it became flooded.

02:54.048 --> 02:55.884
Then I guess Ha-kyung
won't get so much hate.

02:55.967 --> 02:58.011
…underground shops and apartment…

02:58.094 --> 02:59.846
Yes, yes, yes, that's right.

03:00.388 --> 03:04.726
Yes, the typhoon followed
our estimated path fairly closely.

03:05.310 --> 03:08.062
We live with many
different scenarios.

03:08.146 --> 03:10.273
…rainfall also, yes. Uh-huh.

03:11.357 --> 03:12.942
Yes, pretty much. Thanks.

03:13.026 --> 03:14.402
Yes. Yes.

03:15.945 --> 03:19.240
TYPHOON'S PREDICTED PATH CLOSELY MATCHES
WITH THE FORECAST OF THE KMA

03:22.368 --> 03:26.039
Sometimes, the scenario
we prepared for is accurate.

03:33.504 --> 03:35.340
I'm getting up to use the bathroom.

03:42.055 --> 03:44.766
Why did we bring this guy with us anyway?

03:45.850 --> 03:47.310
This was the best course of action.

03:50.521 --> 03:55.526
I want to help fix Si-woo's relationship
with him, as well as ours.

04:06.162 --> 04:07.121
Some things…

04:07.747 --> 04:09.791
are impossible in this life.

04:10.541 --> 04:13.419
Like a person can never stop
a typhoon coming in,

04:13.503 --> 04:15.797
my dad isn't something you can change.

04:16.839 --> 04:20.176
That man will never
put in the work to change.

04:22.804 --> 04:24.806
I need to keep looking out for myself.

04:25.390 --> 04:27.308
I know you'll do the same thing too.

04:32.647 --> 04:33.564
Forgive me.

04:34.857 --> 04:36.317
I can't be what you want.

04:39.904 --> 04:40.822
So let's…

04:43.199 --> 04:44.409
end it.

04:55.837 --> 04:58.923
Sometimes,
the scenario you expected is wrong,

04:59.757 --> 05:02.885
and the actuality causes a catastrophe.

05:07.765 --> 05:09.350
So you came here to negotiate?

05:10.935 --> 05:11.769
I did.

05:17.608 --> 05:18.484
Yu-jin…

05:33.291 --> 05:36.627
The important thing
is that life goes on

05:36.711 --> 05:39.964
whether your scenario was right or wrong.

05:40.048 --> 05:43.301
You heard typhoon 15's
also coming our way, huh?

05:44.052 --> 05:45.928
Uh, judging from the chart…

05:46.012 --> 05:47.513
- Eight hours? Uh-huh?
- Yes.

05:47.597 --> 05:50.641
In eight hours, it'll be on top
of the Korean Peninsula.

05:50.725 --> 05:53.144
So you don't have
to come back up to Seoul.

05:53.227 --> 05:54.771
Just stay there and track the new one.

05:54.854 --> 05:55.938
Huh?

05:56.773 --> 05:58.691
Yeah, of course there. Where else?

05:59.359 --> 06:01.652
The typhoon center,
get over there right now.

06:02.236 --> 06:05.573
- Go on, hurry.
- What? Right now?

06:06.407 --> 06:08.076
Sir, no. I still got to be--

06:14.707 --> 06:16.376
So we have to prepare…

06:17.251 --> 06:20.922
for the next scenario
and the next after that.

06:27.220 --> 06:33.226
EPISODE 13
SCENARIO 1, 2, 3

06:52.161 --> 06:55.665
So when did you find out?

06:55.748 --> 06:56.958
I've known a while.

07:00.169 --> 07:01.003
Hmm?

07:08.094 --> 07:11.305
Whoa! That quickly? Really?

07:12.181 --> 07:14.016
What about you? When did you know?

07:14.100 --> 07:17.478
I had a feeling
for quite a long time, really.

07:24.694 --> 07:26.404
It sounds like you got a cold.

07:26.487 --> 07:27.447
Yeah.

07:27.530 --> 07:30.283
We will now call to order
our meeting for May 10th.

07:30.366 --> 07:31.492
Okay, satellite--

07:33.035 --> 07:35.037
I apol… I apologize.

07:35.121 --> 07:36.998
Um, if you, uh…

07:37.081 --> 07:38.458
Thank… thank you very much.

07:43.212 --> 07:46.090
Oh, my God. No, really. I've got chills.

07:46.174 --> 07:48.926
That's so long ago. Oh, my God!

07:50.052 --> 07:51.345
So how'd you know, then?

07:52.096 --> 07:53.514
Way later than you.

07:54.140 --> 07:55.516
Oh, wait. You know.

08:01.856 --> 08:02.857
Oh.

08:18.915 --> 08:22.043
Yeah, that one was very unsubtle.

08:22.126 --> 08:25.838
I mean, they were so obvious that
it was hard to pretend not to notice.

08:30.801 --> 08:33.179
Stop messing around, okay, Forecaster?

08:33.763 --> 08:34.764
Yes, ma'am.

08:34.847 --> 08:37.141
Oh, they just
wouldn't give it a rest.

08:39.810 --> 08:42.522
So, then, uh, what now from now on?

08:43.105 --> 08:45.107
What do you think? We reveal nothing.

08:45.608 --> 08:49.070
We just keep quiet like we were doing.
Pretend not to know.

08:51.614 --> 08:54.700
Pretend not to know what?

08:54.784 --> 08:57.411
- Huh?
- What? What?

08:57.912 --> 08:59.914
I show up, and now you're all quiet?

08:59.997 --> 09:01.791
No, it's nothing, really.

09:16.347 --> 09:18.266
Forecaster Um knows, right?

09:18.349 --> 09:20.810
Of course, he does.
He went on that retreat.

09:20.893 --> 09:22.895
How oblivious would he
have to be not to know it?

09:24.438 --> 09:25.481
"Oblivious"?

09:27.149 --> 09:28.234
Me, right?

09:28.734 --> 09:29.652
Huh?

09:29.735 --> 09:30.736
Mm-mm.

09:30.820 --> 09:32.196
Uh, no. Not you. Not you.

09:33.573 --> 09:36.659
Wow, you guys hear it all.

09:37.201 --> 09:39.453
It's true. My wife, she wants a divorce.

09:48.337 --> 09:51.173
How on earth did you find out?

09:54.051 --> 09:57.555
Sir, I only have 6,000 won.

09:58.264 --> 10:00.516
Could you please
just take me to the airport?

10:00.600 --> 10:02.560
Please? Hey, please!

10:02.643 --> 10:05.187
Oh, hey! Hey!

10:05.271 --> 10:06.439
Damn it.

10:09.108 --> 10:11.068
Uh, for heaven's sake.

10:14.113 --> 10:16.157
Shit! Damn it.

10:26.250 --> 10:27.585
Hey, Director Lady.

10:28.836 --> 10:30.296
Let me ask you something.

10:32.757 --> 10:35.926
You knew perfectly well that
Si-woo didn't want to see me there,

10:36.010 --> 10:38.512
so why are we in this town?

10:40.681 --> 10:42.016
I also have a question.

10:42.600 --> 10:44.101
Your son's injured.

10:44.185 --> 10:45.853
So how come the money's all you want?

10:47.980 --> 10:50.608
In this world, you gotta watch your nose.

10:50.691 --> 10:52.318
Let your guard down, they'll cut it off.

10:52.401 --> 10:54.362
You let people slide, and they'll get you.

10:54.445 --> 10:56.572
I'm his father.
One of us should keep alert

10:56.656 --> 10:58.824
and get what's ours from this.

11:00.201 --> 11:01.911
So what's the problem?

11:02.953 --> 11:06.082
There are
many different fathers in this world.

11:12.129 --> 11:15.174
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

11:38.531 --> 11:41.075
There are fathers
who try their best,

11:41.158 --> 11:44.453
yet always feel they could do better
for their children.

11:45.663 --> 11:49.709
There are also those irresponsible fathers

11:50.501 --> 11:52.878
who run away, leaving young kids alone.

11:53.796 --> 11:54.714
And there are fathers

11:54.797 --> 11:58.050
who are utterly shameless
and selfish with their children.

12:00.720 --> 12:02.138
Damn it.

12:02.221 --> 12:03.431
Damn it!

12:04.140 --> 12:05.641
I should never have followed you.

12:14.358 --> 12:15.985
You'll have to go to Seoul alone.

13:08.788 --> 13:11.457
Get in. I'll take you to your mom's house.

13:14.668 --> 13:17.338
I really have to talk to you.
Get in the car.

14:18.732 --> 14:21.944
Why are they sending a director
from the main office all the way here?

14:22.486 --> 14:23.863
She doesn't look like
she'll be a lot of help.

14:25.614 --> 14:27.491
If you say so, Director General, I will.

14:28.033 --> 14:29.618
Yes, sir. I know.

14:33.205 --> 14:35.291
Right now, Elisha's
central pressure is 985,

14:35.374 --> 14:37.626
max wind speed
at the center, 27 per second.

14:37.710 --> 14:40.963
It's moving north from the sea
250km south of Jeju.

14:41.046 --> 14:42.047
At this size and speed,

14:42.131 --> 14:44.967
it'll make landfall
on the south coast. And you?

14:45.050 --> 14:46.844
I'll observe the heading.

14:46.927 --> 14:49.221
You stick to synoptic weather observation.

14:50.014 --> 14:50.973
Understood?

14:51.599 --> 14:52.558
Yes, of course.

14:52.641 --> 14:54.768
SYNOPTIC WEATHER OBSERVATION: OBSERVATIONS
MADE AT A SPECIFIC TIME AT ALL STATIONS

14:54.852 --> 14:56.270
How's Forecaster Lee?

14:57.313 --> 14:58.981
Uh, they finished treating him
for the burn.

14:59.064 --> 15:01.150
But with the eye,
they'll have to watch what happens.

15:01.233 --> 15:03.110
Is that so?

15:05.613 --> 15:09.158
Someone got seriously hurt,
and you don't seem to care, huh?

15:14.622 --> 15:19.001
Are you saying your teammate got wounded
because of me?

15:20.753 --> 15:22.546
No, I'm saying

15:22.630 --> 15:26.675
you should at least try to show
some more care and concern for him.

15:30.888 --> 15:32.014
Director Jin.

15:32.806 --> 15:36.185
You've worked at Headquarters
your whole career, right?

15:36.268 --> 15:37.269
Yes. So what?

15:40.147 --> 15:41.523
Do you know what this is?

15:43.692 --> 15:46.403
Baengnokdam, an accident, at the AWS.

15:46.487 --> 15:47.821
I slipped and tore it open.

15:51.450 --> 15:52.868
Assistant Director Park there,

15:52.952 --> 15:55.162
the hearing in his left ear
comes and goes.

15:55.245 --> 15:56.622
He went out on the field
during a rainstorm

15:56.705 --> 15:57.706
and was hit by a street sign.

16:00.000 --> 16:04.296
Mr. Yang here had his car overturned
when he went to observe the wind fields.

16:06.924 --> 16:09.677
Everyone here who's been doing this
longer than ten years

16:09.760 --> 16:11.804
could tell you a similar situation.

16:11.887 --> 16:13.806
I'm sorry that Forecaster Lee got hurt.

16:13.889 --> 16:16.308
But around here, it happens to all of us.

16:17.059 --> 16:19.061
Understand me, Director?

16:21.730 --> 16:22.564
Yes.

16:23.232 --> 16:24.066
Director?

16:26.068 --> 16:28.195
When they say
director around here, it's me.

16:28.278 --> 16:29.780
- Could you?
- Mm-hmm.

16:50.092 --> 16:51.093
What?

16:52.011 --> 16:53.721
Why are you here and not in the hospital?

16:55.514 --> 16:58.100
Turns out it wasn't as bad
as they expected.

16:58.183 --> 17:00.352
And I've always healed pretty quickly.

17:00.436 --> 17:01.812
I thought you hurt your eye too.

17:01.895 --> 17:04.898
They, uh, have to watch it
for three days, that's all.

17:04.982 --> 17:06.817
So far, no problems with it.

17:11.196 --> 17:12.865
Did you hear that, Director?

17:27.254 --> 17:28.505
We need to talk.

17:48.901 --> 17:51.153
No. No more. Enough.

17:51.820 --> 17:53.697
Just be a decent man for once and sign it.

17:53.781 --> 17:57.242
Sign the paper and we can both go on
and move on with our lives.

17:57.951 --> 18:00.079
It's what's best for everyone, yeah?

18:16.595 --> 18:19.098
How's this character?

18:21.433 --> 18:23.352
JIN TAE-KYUNG

18:32.319 --> 18:33.904
Cute.

18:37.116 --> 18:39.451
SAVE

18:48.669 --> 18:51.797
- So the typhoon post is done?
- Oh, uh… No.

18:54.216 --> 18:56.635
- The post is going up now.
- Okay.

19:01.181 --> 19:02.850
See you after work.

19:09.648 --> 19:12.192
TYPHOON REPORT
UPLOADING

19:14.361 --> 19:15.904
Soo-jin, could you
come out a second?

19:20.117 --> 19:21.243
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR PARK SUNG-JIN

19:22.995 --> 19:24.121
Okay.

19:25.664 --> 19:27.541
I'm running over to the Policy Office.

19:27.624 --> 19:28.584
Okay.

19:32.171 --> 19:33.297
GYEOL'S HOMEROOM TEACHER

19:33.380 --> 19:34.298
Oh.

19:34.381 --> 19:37.217
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

19:38.719 --> 19:40.512
Hello. Yes. How are you?

19:41.305 --> 19:43.765
Ah, whoa! He did that? Uh…

19:44.349 --> 19:47.394
Uh, yes. Um… He does that.

19:47.978 --> 19:48.937
Oh.

19:49.897 --> 19:51.315
Yes. Yes, of course.

19:52.232 --> 19:55.527
TYPHOON REPORT
UPLOADING

19:55.611 --> 19:57.237
Go to the hospital.

19:57.821 --> 19:59.489
I've already been discharged.

19:59.573 --> 20:02.117
I'm totally good to work right now.

20:04.870 --> 20:06.663
You do whatever you wanna do, huh?

20:08.874 --> 20:10.500
So let's…

20:11.168 --> 20:12.169
end it.

20:18.133 --> 20:20.385
Just say whatever you want, and that's it?

20:20.969 --> 20:22.846
Okay. Well, you said your part.

20:23.722 --> 20:24.932
But I haven't responded.

20:26.141 --> 20:27.351
So you can just hang on.

20:30.312 --> 20:32.814
Director Jin. You need to come in here.

20:38.195 --> 20:41.365
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION
NATIONAL TYPHOON CENTER

20:42.241 --> 20:43.450
What's going on?

20:44.034 --> 20:45.285
That's what I wanted to know.

20:46.536 --> 20:47.704
What's going on?

20:51.083 --> 20:53.543
Hey, what did you post for the report?

20:53.627 --> 20:56.004
Report? What? Which one?

21:05.973 --> 21:07.557
Hold it. What?

21:08.141 --> 21:09.893
Why is the report a penguin?

21:14.189 --> 21:15.190
Mr. Shin.

21:15.274 --> 21:16.608
Did you upload that?

21:25.575 --> 21:26.910
Go on! Delete it!

21:28.704 --> 21:30.497
Yes… Yes.

21:32.874 --> 21:34.626
Jeez.

21:36.086 --> 21:37.379
TYPHOON REPORT

21:38.797 --> 21:41.049
The typhoon's making landfall,
and this is what they post?

21:41.591 --> 21:43.135
Is this how your department runs?

21:43.218 --> 21:46.471
Not even our day-one hires
would have messed that up.

21:49.558 --> 21:50.517
Is it Mr. Shin?

22:00.319 --> 22:02.070
Yes, hello. What happened?

22:03.280 --> 22:04.489
Mr. Shin…

22:05.407 --> 22:06.658
Um, well…

22:07.326 --> 22:09.411
he uploaded, uh, the wrong file.

22:09.494 --> 22:11.455
It's all my fault.

22:12.247 --> 22:13.707
I was distracted.

22:15.292 --> 22:16.418
No.

22:16.501 --> 22:21.214
I don't know what the penguin's for
or why it's on a work computer.

22:32.309 --> 22:34.227
Okay, Mr. Um, now really,

22:34.311 --> 22:37.147
have you forgotten
you're acting director when I'm gone?

22:38.815 --> 22:41.985
I know you're all happy
about the typhoon 14 analysis.

22:42.069 --> 22:43.403
Another one's almost here.

22:43.487 --> 22:45.697
I'm sorry. I have no excuse.

22:45.781 --> 22:46.782
Oh, uh…

22:46.865 --> 22:48.658
Forgive him, Director. Uh…

22:49.242 --> 22:51.787
Forecaster Um's having
a hard time right now.

22:52.412 --> 22:55.165
His… wife's about to divorce him.

22:56.917 --> 22:58.210
Huh?

22:58.293 --> 23:00.962
I know it's all just so hard for him.

23:01.046 --> 23:02.798
I should
have paid more attention.

23:03.507 --> 23:05.133
It's entirely my fault, Director.

23:05.217 --> 23:06.676
- Why would you say that?
- I'm sorry.

23:06.760 --> 23:09.971
- What if it's on speaker?
- It's my fault, Director.

23:10.055 --> 23:11.223
- Seok-ho, what?
- Give me the phone!

23:11.306 --> 23:13.892
This terrible mistake
in the face of a typhoon is…

23:13.975 --> 23:17.562
Honestly, yes, well,
it's just so inexcusable to me.

23:17.646 --> 23:20.982
Yes, yes, all mine, all my fault.
I'll write a disciplinary report.

23:21.066 --> 23:22.651
- Huh?
- If the report's not enough,

23:22.734 --> 23:24.236
a dock of my pay would be appropriate.

23:24.319 --> 23:25.237
- Don't say that!
- What are you saying?

23:25.320 --> 23:27.489
- No, Director. It's my fault.
- Come on, man! Don't say that.

23:27.572 --> 23:28.949
- I should have checked.
- No. It's my fault.

23:29.032 --> 23:30.742
- No, please!
- I, I just…

23:30.826 --> 23:33.036
- It's not your fault.
- Mr. Um's on the verge of a divorce.

23:33.120 --> 23:34.996
- Assistant Director Oh--
- Everything's my fault.

23:35.080 --> 23:36.623
I can't hear you speak.

23:36.706 --> 23:40.210
Okay, one at a time.
I can't hear any of you!

23:45.841 --> 23:46.758
Yu-jin!

23:47.926 --> 23:50.345
- Don't run, don't run, you'll fall.
- Ki-jun is here.

23:51.471 --> 23:52.389
Really?

24:01.565 --> 24:02.858
Why are you here?

24:03.567 --> 24:05.318
Well, I said I had to talk to you.

24:09.030 --> 24:11.283
- Oh, you're here.
- Here, allow me.

24:11.366 --> 24:12.742
Oh, thanks.

24:12.826 --> 24:14.828
Yu-jin, take this
and go inside and eat.

24:14.911 --> 24:16.997
I'm gonna go and get things for dinner.

24:17.080 --> 24:18.790
Uh, no, it's all right.

24:18.874 --> 24:22.502
Ah, no. You came all the way here.
You need at least one good meal.

24:25.964 --> 24:27.757
Yu-jin.

24:33.763 --> 24:36.600
I don't know what the matter is,
but I do try to placate her.

24:37.267 --> 24:40.395
She's not usually wind up
so tight, you know, hmm?

24:40.479 --> 24:41.396
Sure.

24:47.986 --> 24:49.488
She asked for a divorce.

24:50.071 --> 24:51.448
Out of the blue?

24:54.326 --> 24:56.661
I wouldn't say that, no.

24:58.079 --> 24:59.623
So what did you tell her?

25:00.207 --> 25:01.291
Well, what could I say?

25:01.374 --> 25:02.834
You're just going to go along with it?

25:02.918 --> 25:05.212
She said that I should…

25:05.754 --> 25:07.005
to keep it simple.

25:07.631 --> 25:10.425
I just made her life
very difficult.

25:10.509 --> 25:12.010
And if I try to hold on now,

25:12.594 --> 25:15.180
I'm afraid I'll make it even worse.

25:16.598 --> 25:18.350
You can't just roll over.

25:19.017 --> 25:21.019
How do I change her mind, though?

25:21.102 --> 25:23.271
You need a plan to persuade her
or whatever.

25:23.355 --> 25:24.439
Or just explain.

25:24.523 --> 25:25.607
Wait, how?

25:27.025 --> 25:28.777
You know, three scenarios.

25:36.409 --> 25:38.036
What did you come here for?

25:38.870 --> 25:40.664
To see you, of course.

25:41.289 --> 25:42.916
We can't end this way.

25:42.999 --> 25:44.543
I needed to do something.

25:45.126 --> 25:47.504
What will that be? What else is there?

25:55.512 --> 25:57.764
- Oppa.
- I'm sorry, Yu-jin.

25:58.765 --> 26:01.268
Your oppa's sorry
he caused you pain and hurt you.

26:02.185 --> 26:03.353
He's sorry for everything.

26:03.436 --> 26:05.397
Why are you down there?

26:06.231 --> 26:08.275
Get up.

26:10.443 --> 26:11.528
Okay, stand.

26:11.611 --> 26:13.488
Please let's go back
to Seoul together, Yu-jin.

26:14.948 --> 26:16.116
Get off the ground.

26:16.199 --> 26:19.536
I will as long as you say
you'll come along.

26:28.295 --> 26:29.671
- Come on, get up.
- Mm.

26:30.213 --> 26:31.256
Answer me.

26:31.339 --> 26:33.592
All right, fine! Whatever! Just get up.

26:33.675 --> 26:34.884
You… you mean it?

26:34.968 --> 26:36.928
We're going to go together?
You'll go with me?

26:37.012 --> 26:38.888
Uh-huh, yeah. Get off the grass.

26:40.515 --> 26:41.600
Jeez.

26:57.824 --> 27:01.453
I admit I made a mistake,
but I can't elaborate on why.

27:02.621 --> 27:06.249
I'm sorry. It's personal,
so I can't tell you.

27:09.502 --> 27:12.464
I think my husband is no longer focused.

27:14.174 --> 27:16.801
His Level Five
Civil Service Exam is coming up soon.

27:18.178 --> 27:19.846
And my mother-in-law says

27:19.929 --> 27:21.723
she couldn't take care
of the kids anymore.

27:21.806 --> 27:23.391
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

27:23.475 --> 27:25.143
My wife asked me for a divorce.

27:30.273 --> 27:31.399
So let's…

27:33.652 --> 27:34.819
end it.

27:41.868 --> 27:44.329
What does the GDAPS show?

27:44.412 --> 27:46.414
GDAPS: GLOBAL DATA ASSIMILATION
AND PREDICTION SYSTEM

27:47.457 --> 27:50.502
The speed is increasing
'cause of the rising jet current.

27:50.585 --> 27:53.129
Vertical wind shear is over 50.

27:53.922 --> 27:55.006
Ah, okay.

28:16.361 --> 28:18.530
Did you figure out who sent that file?

28:19.489 --> 28:20.532
Yes, well…

28:20.615 --> 28:23.034
Just another day at Headquarters.

28:24.411 --> 28:27.288
You people over there sit
in your comfy situation room chairs

28:27.372 --> 28:30.041
clicking around all day, so you get weak.

28:32.836 --> 28:35.714
Haven't you ever made
an error like that, Director?

28:37.507 --> 28:41.094
I know that everyone
goes out in the field here,

28:41.177 --> 28:43.847
risking your lives
and getting hurt in the process.

28:43.930 --> 28:45.140
I know.

28:45.223 --> 28:47.517
The situation room's no cake walk either.

28:53.189 --> 28:55.442
Someone's
about to get divorced.

28:57.110 --> 28:59.404
Follow those from there to there.

28:59.487 --> 29:00.655
MOTHER-IN-LAW

29:01.906 --> 29:04.200
Yes, hello.
I'm-- I'm sorry, Mom. I'm working.

29:04.284 --> 29:06.369
One sec, please. Send this to me?

29:06.453 --> 29:07.370
Thanks, sorry.

29:08.371 --> 29:10.457
Someone works
her hands to the bone,

29:10.540 --> 29:14.753
providing for her whole family
but never stops saying sorry.

29:14.836 --> 29:16.296
Yes, I'm sorry. Uh-huh.

29:21.426 --> 29:24.220
Someone has to watch
the seasons go by on the monitor.

29:31.269 --> 29:33.438
Okay. We upload…

29:33.521 --> 29:37.442
Someone's youth is passing by
without a single real relationship.

29:41.279 --> 29:42.739
Are we competing, huh?

29:42.822 --> 29:46.034
Who here has had the worst time
working at the KMA?

29:46.117 --> 29:47.535
No.

29:47.619 --> 29:50.371
I'm saying typhoon center
or situation room,

29:50.455 --> 29:53.249
all of us are working so hard
to get it right here.

29:54.125 --> 29:56.711
So stop trying to so little divisions,

29:56.795 --> 29:59.589
comparing all that
is beneath you, Director.

30:08.306 --> 30:10.600
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

30:10.683 --> 30:13.436
- Get us the scenario analysis.
- Uh, okay.

30:35.166 --> 30:37.418
What are you doing here at this hour?

30:37.502 --> 30:38.378
Uh…

30:40.338 --> 30:41.965
Give me a chance, Hyang-rae.

30:43.633 --> 30:44.843
Just three months.

30:44.926 --> 30:48.304
Let's have a grace period.
Just 90 days, and then…

30:49.514 --> 30:50.598
What does that mean?

30:50.682 --> 30:54.644
Honestly, I… I don't…
I don't think that you're being fair.

30:54.727 --> 30:59.107
So for three months,
let's try and live together.

31:00.149 --> 31:03.069
And then I'll do anything you want, okay?

31:03.152 --> 31:06.948
Huh? If you say you want a divorce,
I'll let you do it.

31:07.031 --> 31:09.576
If you want me
to get out of Seoul, then I'll go.

31:11.035 --> 31:12.954
And what do you want from all that?

31:13.037 --> 31:14.247
It's just that…

31:14.998 --> 31:17.417
Even death row gives you some grace
at the end, huh?

31:18.001 --> 31:22.297
Can't you at least give me just…
just a shred longer, huh?

31:22.380 --> 31:25.258
You have to see I work so hard
for all of us for so long.

31:29.137 --> 31:30.847
Then why are you here and not at work?

31:32.473 --> 31:34.767
I'm on lunch. I ran here.

31:34.851 --> 31:37.604
Then you'll be late.
Go back to your office.

31:37.687 --> 31:39.981
- Oh, honey. Honey.
- Just go, okay?

32:46.339 --> 32:48.049
Hey, hey, Hyang-rae.

32:48.716 --> 32:50.134
What's all this?

32:50.635 --> 32:51.719
Huh?

32:54.931 --> 32:56.432
Oh, that.

32:57.016 --> 32:58.351
Typhoon's landing soon.

32:58.434 --> 33:01.229
Looks like very high winds,
so I put that in.

33:03.982 --> 33:05.024
Are you there?

33:06.859 --> 33:07.860
Hello, honey?

33:07.944 --> 33:10.238
I just can't do three months.

33:11.489 --> 33:12.573
Oh…

33:13.950 --> 33:15.159
'kay.

33:17.662 --> 33:18.788
Two's okay.

33:20.581 --> 33:21.708
"Two"?

33:21.791 --> 33:24.377
Anything you want to do,
do it in those two.

33:24.961 --> 33:28.047
But then, promise me,
you'll get the divorce signed, okay?

33:30.383 --> 33:31.342
Oh.

33:33.136 --> 33:36.097
Yes. Okay. Thanks, Hyang-rae.

33:37.390 --> 33:38.474
I really just…

33:39.308 --> 33:41.477
I'll be good.

33:45.523 --> 33:46.482
Hello?

33:48.359 --> 33:49.944
Hyang-rae, thank you!!

34:13.301 --> 34:14.927
Now.

34:16.179 --> 34:18.806
The linens are new.

34:18.890 --> 34:21.225
- They should be nice and--
- It's great. Thank you.

34:21.309 --> 34:24.312
Oh, the room's a little damp, huh?

34:24.395 --> 34:27.065
If I'd known you were staying,
I could have aired it out a little.

34:27.148 --> 34:29.025
Uh, no it's great, Mama.

34:29.108 --> 34:31.277
Should I turn the boiler on now?
Or should I wait?

34:31.360 --> 34:33.529
No, uh, we'll take care of it.

34:34.405 --> 34:36.115
Oh, okay.

34:36.199 --> 34:37.950
Okay. Go to bed, then.

34:38.034 --> 34:39.911
- Good night.
- Good night. Good night.

34:39.994 --> 34:41.370
- Good night.
- Thank you. Thanks.

34:57.345 --> 34:59.097
I told you to go to a hotel, though.

35:00.807 --> 35:02.016
Uh…

35:02.100 --> 35:05.061
Your father told me to stay the night.
How could I say no?

35:05.728 --> 35:06.771
Not my father.

35:07.480 --> 35:09.357
Stepfathers are fathers too, Yu-jin.

35:09.440 --> 35:10.900
Don't be so harsh.

35:11.609 --> 35:14.403
- I wasn't.
- You're so cold with him.

35:14.487 --> 35:16.781
And you didn't even look at him at supper.

35:16.864 --> 35:18.658
Oppa, what do you know, huh?

35:18.741 --> 35:20.952
I'm not saying that I…

35:21.953 --> 35:24.622
He never knows where he stands with you.

35:24.705 --> 35:27.208
That's what's wrong. He's too nervous.

35:28.584 --> 35:30.378
With my mom and brother, he's so relaxed.

35:30.461 --> 35:34.006
- Well, with you, he has to--
- Yes, I know he's nice.

35:34.090 --> 35:38.136
And he's great with Mom
and a good dad for my little brother also.

35:38.219 --> 35:40.012
I don't have a home here.

35:41.472 --> 35:43.432
It's not my family now, it's theirs.

35:43.975 --> 35:46.727
That's why I wanted
to start a family of my own and yet…

35:46.811 --> 35:48.104
And yet?

35:50.523 --> 35:53.109
Forget it. Let's just sleep.

35:53.192 --> 35:56.070
You're the one who didn't want
to register our marriage.

35:57.947 --> 36:00.324
Do I have to remind you why?

36:00.408 --> 36:02.243
How could I trust you with that?

36:02.326 --> 36:04.620
You care more
about what people think of us,

36:04.704 --> 36:07.165
who that Jin Ha-kyung woman is dating,

36:07.248 --> 36:10.209
and how that will change whatever we have
going on in our relationship.

36:10.293 --> 36:11.460
That's because…

36:12.795 --> 36:15.089
It's because of that Lee Si-woo.

36:15.173 --> 36:17.049
So?

36:17.633 --> 36:19.552
Okay, fine. So what do you most hate?

36:19.635 --> 36:21.387
The fact that I lived with Si-woo?

36:21.470 --> 36:23.598
Or the fact he's dating Jin Ha-kyung?

36:24.182 --> 36:25.224
Both.

36:27.059 --> 36:28.853
Both I find very offensive.

36:28.936 --> 36:30.771
So that's why I want a conclusion.

36:30.855 --> 36:32.690
What's the conclusion, Yu-jin?

36:33.274 --> 36:35.276
You're my wife. So there.
That's our conclusion.

36:35.359 --> 36:36.736
If you regret this, let me know.

36:38.112 --> 36:39.280
We'll forget it.

36:43.659 --> 36:45.286
Are you gonna keep being so mean?

36:45.912 --> 36:48.748
I got down on my knees for you.
So let's move on. Why drag it out?

36:48.831 --> 36:51.209
I'm sorry, but I couldn't live that way.

36:51.292 --> 36:54.712
Pretending we're perfect in front
of everyone like somehow you always do.

36:54.795 --> 36:56.797
Actually, all the time and lying.

36:58.090 --> 36:59.967
I can't do it that way right now.

37:00.051 --> 37:01.594
Do you think I wanna do it like that?

37:01.677 --> 37:03.346
It's just what people do.

37:03.429 --> 37:05.056
That's what married life always is.

37:05.139 --> 37:07.683
But I'm sorry I can't do that
like everyone else in the world.

37:07.767 --> 37:09.185
So then, what do we do?

37:09.268 --> 37:10.228
So let's…

37:11.312 --> 37:14.357
I don't know why you came out here
just to make me feel so awful!

37:17.902 --> 37:19.737
- Honey, stop it!
- What is this?

37:19.820 --> 37:21.197
Are you making my daughter cry?

37:21.280 --> 37:23.616
- Get up, you!
- Sir, no! No! That's not it!

37:23.699 --> 37:25.034
Get out. Let's get out now!

37:25.117 --> 37:26.202
- Hush.
- I…

37:27.453 --> 37:28.955
Ow, ow!

37:30.623 --> 37:33.626
Who said you could make
my daughter cry, huh? Huh?

37:33.709 --> 37:35.253
Sir, that's not it.

37:35.336 --> 37:37.505
Honey, let go and then we'll talk, huh?

37:37.588 --> 37:40.466
I warned you once before at your wedding.

37:40.549 --> 37:44.679
I warned you that if you made
my daughter cry, you die at my hands, huh?

37:44.762 --> 37:45.763
Yeah, you said that.

37:45.846 --> 37:47.014
And then you did!

37:47.098 --> 37:49.558
You've only been married to her
for a few months!

37:49.642 --> 37:51.352
Not a decade. Not even a year.

37:51.435 --> 37:53.229
And already, you got her crying?

37:53.312 --> 37:54.689
- I should--
- Appa! Don't.

37:57.066 --> 37:58.067
What?

37:58.693 --> 37:59.819
"Appa"?

38:01.112 --> 38:02.196
I…

38:03.614 --> 38:06.450
- Oppa, don't, huh?
- Uh…

38:09.120 --> 38:11.497
This is our problem,
and we'll be fine, sir.

38:14.250 --> 38:16.460
- Go in, oppa.
- Okay.

38:16.544 --> 38:17.545
Uh-huh.

38:24.343 --> 38:25.720
You heard it, right?

38:25.803 --> 38:27.888
She said appa. She really said it.

38:30.850 --> 38:34.186
Oh, you go in too.
I'm sure they can solve it themselves.

38:34.270 --> 38:36.605
- Go in.
- But I'm certain she said it.

38:36.689 --> 38:40.443
Okay. She said it. Go in.

38:52.997 --> 38:55.916
Right now, the first
and most likely scenario is

38:56.000 --> 39:00.296
it lands at Jeonnam's south coast
then crosses the Korean Peninsula,

39:00.379 --> 39:03.424
does its wrecking, then at Pohang,
it's back in the ocean.

39:04.216 --> 39:07.053
The second scenario is if it veers east.

39:07.678 --> 39:10.014
This scenario sees less total damage.

39:10.097 --> 39:11.432
However, our southern areas

39:11.515 --> 39:13.309
would have quite
severe destruction regardless.

39:13.392 --> 39:14.894
What about the third?

39:15.478 --> 39:17.563
The North Pacific high contracts.

39:17.646 --> 39:21.525
The typhoon traces the edge there,
south of Jeju Island, turning to Kyushu.

39:21.609 --> 39:25.863
In that case, I would expect it to cause
severe coastal destruction near Busan.

39:26.864 --> 39:29.784
If the high in the North Pacific
contracts just a little further,

39:29.867 --> 39:32.995
it might still veer eastward
as in scenario two, right?

39:35.206 --> 39:37.375
Looking at the current data
for the North Pacific high,

39:37.458 --> 39:38.709
I don't think that would happen.

39:39.794 --> 39:42.380
Uh, Mr. Um, is there a real likelihood

39:42.463 --> 39:44.965
of the typhoon changing course
to the south and growing weaker?

39:45.716 --> 39:48.135
Uh, it's not impossible.

39:48.219 --> 39:52.348
We can't rule out the likely chance
that it could still speed eastward

39:52.431 --> 39:53.766
because of the jet stream in the north.

39:54.934 --> 39:57.770
So it is possible that it could move
along an eastward course?

39:58.354 --> 40:00.689
Yes.
We'll need considerable ground data

40:00.773 --> 40:02.358
to get a thorough report ready for you.

40:03.359 --> 40:05.486
Could we find any more data before that?

40:07.863 --> 40:09.031
Well…

40:14.203 --> 40:16.205
We could launch a sonde
off the eastern side

40:16.288 --> 40:18.499
- and to the west of Jeju.
- And?

40:19.125 --> 40:20.835
Well, you know, it's far too dangerous

40:20.918 --> 40:22.962
to send anyone out in the ocean
to deploy a sonde.

40:23.045 --> 40:26.424
But it's still the best method available
to use at this moment, no?

40:29.468 --> 40:30.344
How's this, then?

40:30.845 --> 40:33.764
We'll deploy a sonde in the east
in Woljeong-ri, at least.

40:33.848 --> 40:36.892
There will be some guessing,
but it's still an improvement from now.

40:37.852 --> 40:39.270
I'll go out to sea for the west one.

40:50.531 --> 40:51.407
Director Jin.

40:51.907 --> 40:53.701
You've never deployed a sonde, have you?

40:54.743 --> 40:55.786
And you wanna take a ship

40:55.870 --> 40:58.414
all the way out there
in this weather and do this?

40:58.998 --> 41:00.583
Director Jin. Listen to me.

41:01.917 --> 41:07.173
Sometimes, it's just not possible
to know everything all of the time.

41:07.256 --> 41:08.799
Do you understand?

41:09.550 --> 41:12.303
Typhoon number 14 was too powerful.

41:12.386 --> 41:14.638
With Elisha right at its heels,

41:14.722 --> 41:16.807
we have to assume
this could be even worse.

41:16.891 --> 41:19.768
Even if they're just predictions,
I believe it's our job to use

41:19.852 --> 41:22.855
the most accurate data
when it's available.

41:27.610 --> 41:29.695
Sir, we can't afford to fail on this.

41:32.490 --> 41:35.534
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

41:52.051 --> 41:55.137
SEOUL, DOKDO, SEOGWIPO
OKINAWA, JAPAN

42:11.028 --> 42:11.904
What is wrong?

42:11.987 --> 42:14.323
You think if you have the ship,
then you can do the sonde?

42:15.074 --> 42:18.327
In these conditions,
remote observation might not work.

42:41.100 --> 42:45.271
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

44:08.437 --> 44:10.481
Meteorology One has arrived at Ieodo.

44:11.440 --> 44:13.150
We're ready for you.

44:13.651 --> 44:15.611
It's going up at 21:00.

44:15.694 --> 44:16.779
Got it.

44:17.696 --> 44:19.990
Director, the wind's too strong after all.

44:20.074 --> 44:21.575
Remote observation won't work.

44:22.159 --> 44:23.827
We'll need to do it manually.

44:27.456 --> 44:28.999
When we go, can you count down?

44:29.083 --> 44:30.292
Mm-hmm, okay.

45:05.452 --> 45:07.371
Five, four…

45:07.454 --> 45:08.997
Three…

45:09.581 --> 45:11.583
two, one!

46:23.113 --> 46:24.948
We got it. It's reporting now.

46:38.796 --> 46:39.630
Okay.

46:39.713 --> 46:41.298
We're getting data from Ieodo.

46:41.381 --> 46:42.966
Oh, really?

46:49.723 --> 46:50.808
Oh…

46:53.477 --> 46:55.229
Did you see what's coming through?

46:55.312 --> 46:56.855
Yes, we're adding it to the array now.

46:56.939 --> 46:58.440
First, we just need to check the NWP.

46:58.524 --> 47:01.026
Send me the data
from the model as soon as it's done.

47:01.109 --> 47:03.070
Okay.

47:03.153 --> 47:04.780
TYPHOON TRACK PREDICTION

47:07.658 --> 47:09.326
Well, I think what you said was true.

47:09.409 --> 47:11.912
If it stays on track,
it will move along Namhae,

47:11.995 --> 47:14.164
and the damages
should be limited to the south.

47:20.838 --> 47:23.465
Did you get the NWP?

47:23.549 --> 47:24.758
Yes, I've got it right now.

47:25.259 --> 47:27.386
Looks like Namhae is where it's headed.

47:27.970 --> 47:28.971
It isn't.

47:30.931 --> 47:32.975
- What?
- That's the data.

47:33.058 --> 47:35.310
But let's just publish the first scenario.

47:35.894 --> 47:37.563
Are you serious?

47:37.646 --> 47:38.939
Yes.

47:39.022 --> 47:41.400
I checked
with Director General Ko already.

47:43.277 --> 47:46.738
Director Jin. You know we're going
to be disciplined for this, don't you?

47:47.531 --> 47:51.076
I'm aware. I'll bear the consequence.

47:51.159 --> 47:54.288
Why would you ever take such a risk?

47:54.371 --> 47:56.456
If the typhoon diverges
from what we publish,

47:56.540 --> 47:59.334
only I'll take the blame, okay?
It's my department.

48:01.587 --> 48:03.130
So can we release?

48:10.220 --> 48:12.931
Okay. We'll publish scenario one.

48:14.224 --> 48:16.310
Good work, Director Jin Ha-kyung.

48:16.393 --> 48:17.352
You as well.

48:26.737 --> 48:29.615
PRESS RELEASE

48:31.658 --> 48:32.492
Huh?

48:33.076 --> 48:34.328
We're exaggerating?

48:35.454 --> 48:36.663
Yeah.

48:36.747 --> 48:39.458
Director Jin said we're going
with scenario one.

48:40.042 --> 48:43.462
I want to stay prepared for the chance
that the northern jet stream

48:43.545 --> 48:44.796
is weaker than we thought,

48:44.880 --> 48:47.883
and the typhoon starts
to head farther to the west.

48:47.966 --> 48:50.469
Still, it's very alarmist, no?

48:50.552 --> 48:52.095
The point of the forecast

48:52.179 --> 48:55.223
is to protect our country
and the people living here.

48:55.307 --> 48:57.976
Not to be perfectly accurate.
That's what I was taught.

48:59.353 --> 49:01.188
All right, Director Jin.

49:01.271 --> 49:04.107
Scenario one's going down the hall
to the press.

49:08.028 --> 49:10.364
TYPHOON ELISHA HEADING NORTH
TO THE SOUTHERN SEA OF JEJU

49:10.447 --> 49:12.699
EXPECTED TO HIT
THE SOUTHERN COAST AT DAWN

49:12.783 --> 49:14.701
News.

49:15.827 --> 49:17.204
News.

49:20.290 --> 49:22.459
News.

49:23.418 --> 49:24.503
Breaking news.

49:24.586 --> 49:28.298
Typhoon No. 15 known as Elisha
is no longer expected to track north,

49:28.382 --> 49:29.800
but instead cross Korea,

49:29.883 --> 49:32.803
making landfall south of Jeonnam
early tomorrow morning.

49:32.886 --> 49:34.137
Elisha is a strong storm

49:34.221 --> 49:36.515
with a central wind speed
of 30m per second.

49:37.265 --> 49:39.726
According to the KMA,
Elisha will be of a similar severity

49:39.810 --> 49:41.353
- as Ricky which preceded it.
- Bo-mi.

49:41.436 --> 49:43.355
You ran home to watch the weather?

49:43.438 --> 49:45.107
- However, its center will pass…
- Yeah.

49:45.190 --> 49:46.692
Appa did this one.

49:46.775 --> 49:48.860
So it is expected
to have a stronger impact.

49:48.944 --> 49:51.697
When did you get so interested
in your father's work?

49:51.780 --> 49:54.366
…also added that citizens
should take special care

49:54.449 --> 49:56.910
against strong winds
and rain throughout the night.

49:59.538 --> 50:00.539
- Mr. Shin.
- Yes, sir?

50:00.622 --> 50:02.040
Take these stats to AD Oh.

50:02.124 --> 50:04.376
- And give me the situation data.
- Okay.

50:06.795 --> 50:09.506
Soo-jin, here,
typhoon information.

50:09.589 --> 50:11.800
- Oh, okay. Uh-huh.
- Can you deliver it? Thank you.

50:16.054 --> 50:18.724
- So from here…
- Yes, like this.

50:18.807 --> 50:20.058
Yeah, that's it.

50:27.649 --> 50:29.109
Okay, that's done.

50:30.027 --> 50:32.904
So we're really going
with scenario one, huh?

50:33.905 --> 50:34.948
Mm-hmm.

50:52.716 --> 50:54.885
Now, it's my turn.

50:56.303 --> 51:00.640
Which scenario do I choose
in this breakup with you?

51:02.309 --> 51:05.062
Scenario one. Cling to him.

51:08.732 --> 51:09.941
Scenario two.

51:10.442 --> 51:12.611
Accept the breakup without a fuss.

51:15.280 --> 51:16.448
Scenario three.

51:17.365 --> 51:21.328
Drag it out and try to get some more time.

51:29.419 --> 51:31.880
So what is it you want?

51:39.387 --> 51:41.264
Give me a little longer.

52:07.791 --> 52:08.875
What is it?

52:09.668 --> 52:11.920
Did something go wrong at work?

52:13.547 --> 52:14.756
I don't think…

52:17.050 --> 52:18.301
I can't do this.

52:19.636 --> 52:20.679
Do what?

52:20.762 --> 52:22.681
I can't see you, Tae-kyung.

52:23.974 --> 52:27.936
I have trouble trying to focus
on more than one thing.

52:28.645 --> 52:29.855
Okay, so?

52:30.438 --> 52:31.273
Ever…

52:31.857 --> 52:34.025
since the first time that I met you,

52:34.734 --> 52:37.779
my priorities have been all turned around.

52:37.863 --> 52:38.864
But…

52:39.447 --> 52:41.449
At the KMA, you won't survive like that.

52:41.533 --> 52:43.952
What was your first priority?

52:44.703 --> 52:46.538
The office, of course, the weather.

52:47.080 --> 52:49.541
So what about now?

53:00.177 --> 53:01.011
Oh?

53:04.764 --> 53:05.974
I…

53:07.017 --> 53:09.352
I'm really not like this at all.

53:09.436 --> 53:10.395
Okay?

53:10.478 --> 53:14.941
I'm… I always have this line
between home and when I go to work.

53:15.025 --> 53:17.319
And I've never once crossed it, okay?

53:17.986 --> 53:21.281
I'm logical and rational, but still, I…

53:21.364 --> 53:22.490
Still, you…

53:24.451 --> 53:26.161
I feel confused and I don't…

53:28.705 --> 53:30.498
I don't know what to do
with all of these feelings.

53:30.582 --> 53:32.167
I can't control and can't shut out.

53:32.667 --> 53:35.503
And if I keep going and make an error,
the citizens will suffer and I'll…

53:35.587 --> 53:38.048
I won't ever forgive myself.
I'll hate myself for it.

53:38.131 --> 53:40.050
And get all swept up in regret and misery.

53:40.133 --> 53:42.594
- And then I'll--
- Shin Seok-ho!

53:42.677 --> 53:43.720
Yes?

53:54.856 --> 53:55.690
Oh!

54:01.571 --> 54:03.823
I also like you!

54:07.661 --> 54:08.745
Oh, really?

54:11.957 --> 54:13.667
You haven't had dinner yet, right?

54:14.167 --> 54:16.169
Let's do mung bean pancakes
with rice wine.

54:16.253 --> 54:17.629
Let's go.
Has the rain stopped?

54:23.969 --> 54:25.595
Wait. Don't leave yet. I…

54:31.476 --> 54:32.644
I'm coming!

54:56.543 --> 54:58.211
- Yeah!
- Oh, yeah!

54:58.295 --> 55:00.380
If only I can fix my life
with a swing, huh?

55:00.463 --> 55:02.215
Yeah, you're on a roll today.
You're crazy.

55:05.510 --> 55:07.137
Yeah!

55:11.224 --> 55:13.268
- Yeah, another one, huh?
- Yeah, sure.

55:14.185 --> 55:15.520
- Here, right? I get a point.
- Oh, yeah!

55:15.603 --> 55:17.355
- One more, huh? Another?
- Oh, yeah!

55:24.571 --> 55:25.780
How come you're out here?

55:27.282 --> 55:28.908
What are you doing here, Myung-ju?

55:29.492 --> 55:31.411
See? I told you I saw Appa go out.

55:31.494 --> 55:33.705
I said he went down to the batting cages.

55:33.788 --> 55:35.915
Yesterday and the day before that too.

55:35.999 --> 55:38.043
Right, Appa? Did I get it right?

55:55.435 --> 55:57.896
You have, um, three scenarios.

55:59.314 --> 56:00.398
"Scenarios"?

56:00.982 --> 56:01.941
Number one.

56:02.567 --> 56:03.735
Get your old job again.

56:04.361 --> 56:06.154
- Honey.
- Two.

56:06.946 --> 56:08.239
I divorce you.

56:09.366 --> 56:10.867
- Honey!
- Three.

56:11.659 --> 56:13.244
You're gonna study your ass off.

56:20.668 --> 56:23.922
Do you think I'm running this family
because I have an abundance of energy?

56:24.005 --> 56:27.258
It's because you've got this dream,
and even now, at our age,

56:27.342 --> 56:29.427
I wanted you to try it
before time ran out.

56:30.053 --> 56:31.930
So you wouldn't live with regrets.

56:32.013 --> 56:34.641
It's so difficult. I'm so tired.

56:35.475 --> 56:37.185
But I thought this was the only shot.

56:37.685 --> 56:39.521
So I said that you should give it a try.

56:40.647 --> 56:41.606
And now what?

56:42.816 --> 56:44.150
You're too stressed?

56:51.783 --> 56:55.245
Aren't you the slightest bit ashamed
about all of it, giving me your lies

56:55.328 --> 56:57.080
and ignoring our kids?

57:05.213 --> 57:07.257
And what about your mother, then, huh?

57:07.340 --> 57:10.093
She used to watch our two little boys
every day of the month.

57:15.974 --> 57:16.850
Myung-ju.

57:17.851 --> 57:18.893
I'm very sorry.

57:20.186 --> 57:21.396
I was terrible.

57:25.817 --> 57:26.734
Choose, then.

57:28.111 --> 57:30.905
Scenario one, two, or three?

57:40.248 --> 57:43.418
What is happening? Why is there sun?

57:43.501 --> 57:46.421
Typhoon number 15, Elisha,
which was expected to hit the country

57:46.504 --> 57:47.755
early this morning.

57:47.839 --> 57:50.300
- It crossed the South Sea at four…
- Bo-mi, have you been here all night?

57:50.383 --> 57:51.593
…in the morning
in the eastern seas…

57:51.676 --> 57:55.555
- I'm so… annoyed.
- What? Why?

57:55.638 --> 57:56.473
The news.

57:56.556 --> 57:58.016
…extra tropical cyclones

57:58.099 --> 57:59.601
and eventually fade away.

58:00.393 --> 58:05.023
Unlike the forecast from the KMA
which showed the typhoon battering Korea…

58:05.106 --> 58:07.525
- …it passed by without incidents.
- Oh, the forecast?

58:07.609 --> 58:11.988
Why did he get it wrong?
He was spot on with Number 14.

58:12.572 --> 58:14.532
Getting it perfect isn't the point.

58:14.616 --> 58:17.785
The typhoon passed with barely any damage,
that's what counts.

58:21.623 --> 58:22.457
What?

58:23.416 --> 58:24.626
Goosebumps.

58:25.627 --> 58:26.836
What was that, Mom?

58:26.920 --> 58:30.715
I thought there is nothing between you
since you were apart for so long.

58:31.299 --> 58:32.425
And?

58:32.509 --> 58:34.385
You sounded just like a KMA employee.

58:35.803 --> 58:38.139
That's ridiculous.
Go and get ready for school.

58:38.223 --> 58:39.599
We'll have breakfast in a minute.

58:43.478 --> 58:44.896
Honey.

58:45.939 --> 58:46.814
Bo-mi.

58:47.398 --> 58:48.775
I brought hangover soup for us.

58:49.484 --> 58:50.818
Hangover soup?

58:50.902 --> 58:51.986
What?

58:52.070 --> 58:53.821
You used to love this
when you were little.

58:55.532 --> 58:56.908
That was a long time ago.

58:56.991 --> 58:59.410
I know. And that place is actually
still selling the same soup.

58:59.994 --> 59:02.539
There were tons of people there.
You haven't had breakfast, huh?

59:02.622 --> 59:05.208
You don't need to heat anything up.
We can eat now. Come on.

59:07.669 --> 59:11.214
I asked them
for a lot of blood pudding.

59:12.799 --> 59:13.841
'Cause it's so great.

59:13.925 --> 59:16.469
It smells good.

59:17.178 --> 59:19.889
Right? Uh, bowls?

59:19.973 --> 59:21.349
- Here.
- Oh, thanks.

59:22.141 --> 59:23.560
Some spoons also. Yeah.

59:26.521 --> 59:27.772
See this?

59:29.232 --> 59:30.400
Too small?

59:31.693 --> 59:33.903
Huh? No, just eat.

59:33.987 --> 59:36.531
- Wait, we need spoons.
- Here.

01:00:03.182 --> 01:00:04.267
Huh?

01:00:24.537 --> 01:00:26.414
Well, what do you know.

01:00:39.302 --> 01:00:40.428
Put this on.

01:00:55.360 --> 01:00:56.527
So how is your eye?

01:01:01.532 --> 01:01:02.784
It feels fine.

01:01:03.409 --> 01:01:05.662
You didn't have to follow me out to sea.

01:01:08.706 --> 01:01:09.624
I told you.

01:01:09.707 --> 01:01:12.251
It's very technical, sending up a sonde.

01:01:15.213 --> 01:01:16.381
And I also…

01:01:17.131 --> 01:01:18.800
agreed with what you said earlier

01:01:19.550 --> 01:01:23.554
about Elisha heading to the east
instead of across Korea.

01:01:27.225 --> 01:01:29.102
I came because I wanted to check it out.

01:01:29.644 --> 01:01:31.145
That's the only reason.

01:01:35.692 --> 01:01:37.151
You'll do okay on your own?

01:01:40.863 --> 01:01:44.534
Do you think we can work together
even after it's over?

01:01:47.412 --> 01:01:50.498
Are you gonna be okay on your own?

01:02:02.760 --> 01:02:04.053
Yeah, I think so.

01:02:06.180 --> 01:02:07.432
I'll be fine.

01:02:11.561 --> 01:02:12.937
Let's just end it.

01:02:19.652 --> 01:02:21.279
We're over now, Si-woo.

01:02:35.585 --> 01:02:36.627
Okay, sure.

01:02:48.639 --> 01:02:53.227
Typhoons happen
to release the thermal imbalance

01:02:53.311 --> 01:02:54.729
from the Earth's rotation.

01:02:58.775 --> 01:03:02.820
Unlike the typhoon forecast
that the authorities gave us earlier,

01:03:02.904 --> 01:03:04.697
it was a non-existent storm.

01:03:04.781 --> 01:03:07.450
- Polls are showing…
- Yes, I'm sorry. Yes.

01:03:07.533 --> 01:03:11.037
- …lowers faith in the KMA.
- Ah, yes. Yes, I see it. Yes.

01:03:11.621 --> 01:03:12.955
KMA'S TYPHOON MIS-FORECAST

01:03:13.039 --> 01:03:14.165
SHAMEFUL TYPHOON WARNING

01:03:14.248 --> 01:03:15.082
Well…

01:03:15.166 --> 01:03:17.126
YOU SAID THE TYPHOON WAS COMING!
WHERE IS ELISHA?

01:03:19.921 --> 01:03:20.797
Yes.

01:03:21.798 --> 01:03:24.759
Yes. I will report right back.

01:03:34.769 --> 01:03:37.021
STOP EXCESSIVE FORECASTS.
WE WANT AN ACCURATE WEATHER REPORT.

01:03:38.022 --> 01:03:41.818
The typhoon might
make this harder for us now, but…

01:03:50.993 --> 01:03:55.998
in the long run, it's good as it renews
the water for our environment.

01:04:16.686 --> 01:04:17.770
As long…

01:04:19.272 --> 01:04:22.191
as we can just survive that moment.

01:04:25.194 --> 01:04:28.281
DOMESTIC FLIGHTS

01:04:43.379 --> 01:04:44.672
I'll see you at the office.

01:04:48.801 --> 01:04:50.094
Should I bring your stuff to you?

01:04:51.262 --> 01:04:52.221
I'll…

01:04:52.305 --> 01:04:54.265
come get them on my next weekend.

01:04:56.225 --> 01:04:57.184
Sounds good.

01:04:58.811 --> 01:04:59.854
Okay.

01:05:34.555 --> 01:05:37.391
Why so nervous? I mean, it's our house.

01:05:47.360 --> 01:05:48.402
Come on.

01:06:08.965 --> 01:06:13.427
LIQUID IRON SUPPLEMENT FOR PREGNANT WOMEN

01:06:13.511 --> 01:06:16.097
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:06:18.599 --> 01:06:21.060
- Have a good meal.
- Oh. Thanks, you too.

01:06:25.982 --> 01:06:27.191
Si-woo.

01:06:28.734 --> 01:06:30.152
Oh, yeah.

01:06:33.906 --> 01:06:36.534
Well, I heard
that you're dating Director Jin.

01:06:37.785 --> 01:06:38.786
What?

01:06:38.869 --> 01:06:41.372
I feel so bad, so sorry.

01:06:41.455 --> 01:06:44.959
I must have gotten in the way
when we both stayed over with her.

01:06:45.042 --> 01:06:47.003
So when did it start? While we were there?

01:06:48.587 --> 01:06:51.549
Uh, wait, no, uh…
Who did you hear that from?

01:06:51.632 --> 01:06:53.259
Nobody, really.

01:06:53.342 --> 01:06:55.720
Everyone on the team knew. I was the last.

01:06:56.721 --> 01:06:58.431
Everyone… How?

01:06:58.514 --> 01:06:59.807
I don't know.

01:07:00.391 --> 01:07:02.727
You know,
you're pretty brave, aren't you?

01:07:02.810 --> 01:07:07.773
Of all people, our director
while we all work together, man. Gosh!

01:07:07.857 --> 01:07:09.734
Forecaster Lee is dating Director Jin.

01:07:09.817 --> 01:07:11.861
But no, for real, though.

01:07:12.737 --> 01:07:14.613
Good for the two of you.

01:07:15.322 --> 01:07:18.159
You guys
are great together. Congratulations!

01:07:18.242 --> 01:07:21.287
I'm serious. I was just teasing.

01:07:21.370 --> 01:07:23.205
And I am sorry.

01:07:23.289 --> 01:07:25.624
I was so oblivious, wasn't I, huh?

01:07:25.708 --> 01:07:28.419
Is he dating Director Jin?

01:07:28.502 --> 01:07:31.505
- Oh, good for them.
- Yeah.

01:07:33.174 --> 01:07:34.675
Congratulations!

01:07:58.908 --> 01:08:01.160
Director! Director!

01:08:11.921 --> 01:08:13.130
Are you here for your stuff?

01:08:13.214 --> 01:08:15.299
I told you I'd bring it to you. Hang on.

01:08:15.382 --> 01:08:16.592
Hey, something's wrong.

01:08:17.843 --> 01:08:18.761
What?

01:08:18.844 --> 01:08:20.638
They found out about the two of us.

01:08:21.722 --> 01:08:22.807
Wha… what?

01:08:22.890 --> 01:08:24.517
That we've been together.

01:08:25.434 --> 01:08:26.268
Huh?

01:08:26.352 --> 01:08:28.479
That I was dating you!

01:08:28.562 --> 01:08:31.107
Everybody knows about what went on
between the two of us.

01:08:31.190 --> 01:08:32.399
What?

01:08:32.983 --> 01:08:34.026
Eomma!

01:08:38.405 --> 01:08:41.325
I just knew. I knew.

01:08:41.408 --> 01:08:42.785
So you two had a little

01:08:42.868 --> 01:08:46.080
- office romance, didn't you?
- Eomma, no, I--

01:08:46.163 --> 01:08:49.333
Oh, I really just knew
something was going on.

01:08:50.668 --> 01:08:53.003
- No way! We're not--
- Not what, huh?

01:08:56.715 --> 01:08:59.009
And I also knew that you would deny it.

01:08:59.093 --> 01:09:01.929
So I brought my undeniable proof.

01:09:09.061 --> 01:09:10.521
Take a good look.

01:09:10.604 --> 01:09:11.981
Still deny it?

01:09:59.862 --> 01:10:02.823
People are taking it
more seriously than they should.

01:10:03.741 --> 01:10:06.619
Ignore them.
Don't listen to them or reply.

01:10:06.702 --> 01:10:08.954
But I made dumpling soup, your favorite.

01:10:09.038 --> 01:10:10.539
I just have a stomachache.

01:10:10.623 --> 01:10:13.751
I thought he'd be much more mature.
But he turned out to be a baby.

01:10:13.834 --> 01:10:15.252
You must really love him.

01:10:15.920 --> 01:10:17.338
We broke up.

01:10:17.922 --> 01:10:20.341
You can't maintain
a relationship if it's one-sided.

01:10:20.424 --> 01:10:23.052
Hey! Where should we go?

01:10:23.135 --> 01:10:24.803
I have something to tell you.

01:10:24.887 --> 01:10:28.098
To be honest, Forecaster Lee and I…
